# Local env files — NEVER commit these.
# A tracked .env.local is what broke production: it carried
# APP_BACKEND_URL=http://localhost:3000, Next loaded it at build time (Netlify
# build env vars only override the keys they define), and every /api/* rewrite
# was pointed at localhost inside the Lambda. .env.example is the documented
# template and is the only env file that belongs in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
